B2 mutation check, 2026-11-07 06:06 UTC
Each mutant injects one bug into a copy of the RTL; tb_mesh (4x4) runs every test with +SEED=1 +N03_REPS=1 +N08_CYCLES=20000.
full    = RTL assertions on (normal build)
tb-only = RTL assertions compiled out (+define+SYNTHESIS): only testbench checks can kill it
Killed = the run fails (RESULT FAIL, a $fatal, a hang, or no RESULT line). 'in Nxx' = the last test the run reached:
for a $fatal that is where it stopped; after an ERROR the run goes on to the end (N08), and the ERROR line names
what failed. M10 survives tb-only as expected: a body flit 're-allocates' the VC its packet already holds, which
changes no state; only the output unit's allocation assertion sees it (an equivalent mutant).

